$DIR/main.p:17:10: cannot keep the closure counterFrom(n) returns past this iteration of the loop: it is stored in last, declared outside the loop (main.p:15)
    A function that returns a closure builds it in a region its caller provides
    (spec section 4.5). The region of a call in a loop is part of this frame,
    and the call uses the same region on every iteration, so the closure
    counterFrom(n) returns on one iteration is overwritten on the next. Keeping
    it past the iteration, in last, declared outside the loop (main.p:15), would
    leave it changing under you.
    Use the closure within the iteration, or declare the variable that holds it
    inside the loop.
    Go allocates each closure on the heap. Plutonium builds it in the caller's
    frame, which has room for one closure per call site.
    (see "Closures do not outlive their frame" in the Plutonium spec, section
    4.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3101" for a longer explanation)

